    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Epic Systems is a healthcare software company founded in 1979 and headquartered in Verona. Its website says it was founded in a basement in 1979 and that it develops software to help people get well, stay well, and help future generations be healthier.\n\nThe company's AI work is described on its site as built directly into Epic. It describes an AI-supported outpatient office visit that helps clinicians arrive prepared, anticipates what they need in the room, and lines up documentation and orders for clinician review before the visit ends. It also describes Chart with Art, which it calls Epic's native AI charting, and says clinicians report improved focus on the conversation in the room when it handles documentation. The site states that clinicians at Memorial Hermann Health System are using an AI tool built into Epic to help patients better understand their test results and make informed decisions about next steps in their care.\n\nEpic's tracked product is Epic AI, which includes SlicerDicer, listed under healthcare and life sciences AI. The notes on that product flag clinical decision support, patient data exposure, HIPAA as critical, and FDA software as a medical device considerations. No litigation, MCP servers, SEC filings, or patent facts are recorded for the company.",
